From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cuttlely vendor <vendor@cuttlely.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cuttlely: MCP retry, rediscovery and circuit breaker scope

What: tools/mcp_tool_cuttlely.py holds the logic; tools/mcp_tool.py, mcp_tool_discovery.py and mcp_tool_handlers.py call it through short hooks. A startup tools/list that returns nothing or cannot connect is retried, a call that finds the server toolless rediscovers its tools, and an MCP result with cuttlelyOutcome "expected" stays off the circuit breaker. Real transport failures still open it, per chat when the call has a session id. The analyst tool call also receives that session id as _cuttlelyScope, so a page cursor cannot be reused from another chat; the Cuttlely bridge removes it before the tool schema. tests/tools/test_cuttlely_mcp_retry.py covers it.

Why: Cuttlely's MCP bridge starts alongside Hermes, so the first tools/list can be empty, and an expected analyst refusal must not take the analyst tool away for every chat.
